The rule states that `recovered-from-prose` is 'no' if the harness could "read it as strict JSON" [a70c2e9bc362b532]. In the source, `parse_content` only returns `False` for `recovered_from_prose` if `loads_strict(content)` succeeds (line 85). Since Markdown fences are not valid JSON, any input containing them will result in `recovered_from_prose` being 'yes', regardless of whether the content inside the fence is a clean JSON object.

This failure matters because it reveals a misunderstanding of the boundary between the raw reply and the recovered object. A proposer should next try to test the transition from a fenced object to a bare object (without fences), as that is the only way to move `recovered-from-prose` to 'no'.

